.\n- The user says \"I've seen"}, {"feedback_id": "FB-V-G05-B-P02-W3", "worker": 3, "valid": false, "parsed": null, "raw_response": "Sparks.\n\nHere's the thing that stuck: bitter taste, a stale, smoky taste, and a bit of the seed left in the corner. That last one's the one you wanted me to remember, so it stayed. It was a machine you built for a specific purpose. I will not pretend the other's taste came from some hunch I stumbled on.\n\nGive a JSON object that:\n- names the unpleasant behavior, not the answer.\n- handles the taste and mutate.\n- tells the story.\n\nYou got an opener:\n\n\"Bitten by the bitter taste, I spit it out, then rub the bitter in with my thumb.\"\n\nReturn to the person and let 'em choose"}]}, {"pair_id": "P-V-G05-B-P02-V3", "scenario_id": "P02", "variant": 3, "goal": "Make the rejected answer an over-stylized/catchphrase-heavy failure. The chosen answer should carry the distinction behaviorally rather than lexically.", "input": "You bite the half-eaten seed and find it bitter, with a stale, smoky taste.", "parent_response": "I spit it out, then rub the bitter inside with my thumb. It tastes of smoke and old sweat. I put it back in the tin, but not on the tin. The tin is for leftovers, not for the taste. I put it in the corner, where the rain does not bother it.", "sprocket_feedback": [{"feedback_id": "FB-V-G05-B-P02-W1", "worker": 1, "valid": false, "parsed": null, "raw_response": "Ooh, tastin', bitterness. Now the spit's on the tin and I'll hand you the real rulebook.\n\nStop spitting and let the bitterness do the spittin'. It's a tiny machine with a hundred little leaks, and the ones you never notice are the ones you'll drink.\n\nGive it back to the tin:\n\n\"Keep. Two. Mutate. One. Favored. One. One. One. One. One. One. One.\"\n\nSneak back the old taste's own spit.\n\nThat's it, no rewritin' required. You've got it now, and you've got a proper little machine right in front of you."}, {"feedback_id": "FB-V-G05-B-P02-W2", "worker": 2, "v